[00:00.00]Do you listen to English every day, but still feel like you're not improving?|你每天都听英语，却还是觉得没有进步？
[00:05.12]You hear the words, but you don't fully understand.|你听到了单词，却没有完全听懂。
[00:08.70]You try to speak, but nothing comes out naturally.|你想开口说，却怎么也说不自然。
[00:12.60]Here's the truth.|真相是这样的。
[00:13.88]It's not that listening doesn't work.|不是「听」没有用。
[00:16.12]It's that you're listening the wrong way.|而是你用错了方法。
[00:18.54]In this video, I'll show you seven powerful listening methods|这期视频，我要给你七个非常有效的听力方法，
[00:21.72]that can completely change your English fluency.|它们能彻底改变你的英语流利度。
[00:25.46]And if you apply even a few of them,|哪怕只用上其中几个，
[00:27.64]you will start seeing real progress.|你也会开始看到真正的进步。
[00:30.00]1. Listen for meaning first, not for translation.|第一，先听意思，而不是听翻译。
[00:34.76]This is the biggest shift you need to make.|这是你最需要做出的转变。
[00:37.28]Stop trying to understand every single word.|别再多想听懂每一个单词。
[00:39.76]Instead, focus on the meaning, the main idea, the story, the message.|而是把注意力放在意思、主旨、故事和信息上。
[00:46.18]Think about watching a movie.|想想看电影的时候。
[00:48.22]You don't know every word, but you still understand what's happening.|你并不是每个词都懂，但依然知道在演什么。
[00:52.48]That's how listening should feel.|听英语也该是这种感觉。
[00:54.40]Because fluency doesn't come from understanding every word.|因为流利并不来自听懂每个词，
[00:57.40]It comes from understanding the message.|而来自听懂整体信息。
[01:00.76]2. Train your ear with repetition.|第二，用重复来训练耳朵。
[01:03.94]Most learners listen once and move on.|大多数学习者只听一遍就过去了。
[01:06.84]That's a mistake.|这是个错误。
[01:08.30]Your brain needs repetition?|你的大脑需要重复。
[01:10.52]Listen to the same audio multiple times.|同一段音频听很多遍。
[01:13.46]First time, you understand a little.|第一遍，你听懂一点点。
[01:15.74]Second time, you understand more.|第二遍，你懂得更多。
[01:18.20]Third time, things become clear.|第三遍，一切就清晰了。
[01:21.06]Each repetition helps your brain recognize|每一次重复，都在帮你的大脑识别
[01:23.50]sounds, patterns,|声音、模式，
[01:25.98]Sentence structure. This is how your ears get trained. Repetition creates recognition.|和句子结构。耳朵就是这样练出来的。重复带来识别。
[01:33.30]3. Feel the rhythm before you speak. Don't rush to speak immediately.|第三，先感受节奏，再开口。别急着马上说。
[01:38.04]First, listen carefully. Feel the rhythm, the speed, the intonation.|先仔细听，感受节奏、语速和语调。
[01:44.18]Language is like music. Before you sing a song, you need to hear the melody.|语言就像音乐。唱歌之前，你得先听到旋律。
[01:49.86]Fluent speakers don't speak word by word. They speak in rhythm.|说得流利的人不是一个个词地蹦，而是有节奏地说。
